<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to June 28.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to June 28.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to June 28 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week June 22-June 28</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97	 110,364 tns	 13,086 tns    10.86 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	  49,733 tns	  4,416 tns     8.88 pct</p>
<p>     94-95	  76,798 tns	  7,343 tns     9.56 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to June 28</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    42,101,670 tns    4,539,524 tns    10.78 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    40,117,665 tns    4,372,126 tns    10.90 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    40,079,127 tns    4,273,434 tns    10.66 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 8 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 2 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 6 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
</text>
